# Divisions and remainders by a constant in SPIR-V (src/idrw.c through
# simplify): with the dividend bounded by the request's assumption they
# become one multiply and one shift where the model prices that lower.
SAT simplify x in [0, 1000) nofile
```glsl
uint Dec(uint x) { return x / 10u + x % 10u * 16u; }
int Q(int x) { return (x * 31 + 127) / 255; }
int R(int x) { return x % 7; }
```
# a model where a multiply is dear: the divisions stay
model muldear : gt1030 { imul: 20 }
use muldear
SAT simplify x in [0, 1000) nofile
```glsl
uint Dec(uint x) { return x / 10u + x % 10u * 16u; }
```
# no bound on the dividend: nothing is derived
use gt1030
SAT simplify nofile
```glsl
uint Dec(uint x) { return x / 10u + x % 10u * 16u; }
```
